        'body'    => "## Mission\n\nEAIFR was established in 2018 as a young and dynamic international hub for higher education and research in basic sciences in Africa. Thanks to a tripartite agreement between the University of Rwanda, UNESCO and the government of Rwanda, it is a category 2 institute under the auspices of UNESCO. It operates as a research and teaching institute affiliated to the University of Rwanda with the Abdus Salam International Centre for Theoretical Physics (ICTP) as a partner institute.\n\n## Vision\n\n- Create a community of African scientists in an international network for basic science.\n- Address African challenges in natural hazards, energy, climate, materials and health.\n- Deliver academic excellence — quality over quantity.\n\n## Governance & partnerships\n\nEAIFR has two levels of governance. The first is the Steering Committee which is made up of representatives of the Rwanda Ministry of Education, the University of Rwanda, the ICTP, and other stakeholders. The Steering Committee sets general guidelines for the institute's activities, determines budgeting levels, and considers proposals from the Director for the programme, work plans, financial plans, and budget.\n\nThe second is the Scientific Council which is composed of distinguished scientists in the areas of interest to the institute. This council advises EAIFR on its programmes of activities, taking into consideration major academic, scientific, educational and cultural trends relevant to the institute's objectives.\n\n### ICTP-EAIFR Steering Committee\n\n- Mike Hughes — MINEDUC Representative; Steering Committee Chair\n- Dr. Amal Kasry — UNESCO Representative; Steering Committee Member\n- Dr. Raymond Ndikumana — University of Rwanda (UR), UR Vice-Chancellor's Representative; Steering Committee Member\n- Dr. Ralf Kaiser — Director of Programs, ICTP\n- Chair of the EAIFR Scientific Council — invited ex officio\n- Director of EAIFR — Secretary\n\nThe IUCEA representative from the University of Dar es Salaam is to be confirmed.\n\n### EAIFR Scientific Council\n\nMembership to be confirmed soon.",
