        'summary' => "How to apply to ICTP-EAIFR's master's programme in physics.",
        'body' => "The University of Rwanda (UR) through the ICTP-East African Institute for Fundamental Research (EAIFR) is offering a two-year Masters programs in Physics with specializations in Condensed Matter Physics, Geophysics, and High Energy Physics. The quality of the Masters courses will be at the same level as the Postgraduate Courses given at the International Centre for Theoretical Physics (ICTP) in Trieste Italy. In the first year, students take the same basic physics courses designed to bring them to an advanced level in preparation for the second year in which they specialize into one of the three areas mentioned above. Students who successfully complete their programs will obtain a master's degree in physics from the University of Rwanda.\n\n## Mode of attendance\n\nBy full-time course work (offered by modules) and a final thesis at the end of the second year. All courses will be given at the ICTP-EAIFR building on the UR Nyarugenge campus in Kigali, Rwanda.\n\n## Minimum qualifications\n\nBachelors degree with honours in Physics or Maths with distinction. The selection of candidates will be based on their university record and on academic recommendations.\n\n## Funding\n\n- A limited number of scholarships are available for the top performing students.\n- The [University fee structure](https://eaifr.ictp.it/media/30305/revised-postgraduate-tuition-and-administrative-fees.pdf) can be consulted online.\n\n## Documents required for application\n\n1. A cover letter which should contain the candidate's motivation to join the program.\n2. Detailed curriculum vitae.\n3. Copies of academic certificates (notarised copies will be required before admission).\n4. Copies of academic transcripts (original/notarised transcripts will be required before admission).\n5. Two recommendation letters from academic referees who are knowledgeable about the applicant and their studies.\n6. Documents that give proof of the student's ability to follow advanced-level courses, study and write scientific literature in the English language.\n7. Copy of national identity card or passport.\n\n## How to apply\n\n### Through the ICTP portal\n\n**Please use the ICTP portal.**\n\n1. Go to the [ICTP application portal](https://e-portal.ictp.it/applicant/login).\n2. Create an account if you do not already have one and fill in your personal profile.\n3. Fill in and submit the online application form.\n\n### Through the UR Centre for Postgraduate Studies (CPGS)\n\n1. Go to the [University of Rwanda website](https://www.ur.ac.rw/).\n2. Go to \"Admission\", \"Applicant Portal\" and click \"New Application\".\n3. Fill the Biographical Form and click \"Save\". At the end you will get your Student ID Reference Number and create a PIN.\n4. Keep this ID number, as it will be your identification for all transactions at UR.\n5. Submit all required documents using the [UR document submission portal](http://pgfile.ur.ac.rw/pgfile/findme.php).\n\n**All documents must be in PDF.** If all required documents are not submitted you will not be able to go to the next step. When your submission succeeds, you will find a message in your email box.\n\n## Further information\n\nFor additional information, clarifications or inquiries, please contact:\n\n- Centre for Postgraduate Studies Officer: admissions.pgs [at] ur.ac.rw\n- ICTP-East African Institute for Fundamental Research: admin-assist [at] eaifr.org\n\n[Master's programme](/academics/msc-physics) · [Frequently asked questions](/msc-faqs)",
